## Context
~/CNRS/code/VN-Power-Scenario is a git repo on branch master. It has two remotes: `origin`, the author's own github.com/MinhHaDuong/VN-Power-Scenario, and `fork`, github.com/alice-dub/VN-Power-Scenario, a collaborator's repository. It has requirements.txt, a Makefile with `PYTHON = python3`, no pyproject.toml and no uv.lock. Observed 2026-10-23: 22 uncommitted files.

Practice to reach: `rules/coding-python.md` (Environment principles and rules), tracked by 1206.

## Constraints
Do not push to the `fork` remote or open anything in the collaborator's repository without the author's go: whether the collaborator wants this change is the author's call. Work in a git worktree: the 22 uncommitted files stay untouched.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] pyproject.toml and a committed uv.lock describe the dependencies; no hand-kept requirements.txt
- [ ] the Makefile has no PYTHON variable; recipes that run Python tools go through the `RUN` prefix
- [ ] no `pip install` in the Makefile, README or docs/
- [ ] the repo's own tests or smoke command pass from a bare shell, output quoted in the PR or log
